      "title": "Content",
      "content": [
        "# WordPress.com Deployment Tools\r",
        "\r",
        "These batch files help simplify the process of deploying your WordPress child theme changes from local development to WordPress.com using GitHub Deployments.\r",
        "\r",
        "## Files Included\r",
        "\r",
        "1. **push-to-github.bat** - Push your committed changes to GitHub\r",
        "2. **prepare-pull-request.bat** - Generate a pull request URL and open it in browser\r",
        "3. **wp-deploy-guide.bat** - Step-by-step guide for deploying to WordPress.com\r",
        "4. **sync-all-themes.bat** - Sync theme files to Local by Flywheel\r",
        "5. **export-theme.bat** - Create a .zip file of your child theme for manual upload\r",
        "\r",
        "## Deployment Workflow\r",
        "\r",
        "### Step 1: Develop locally\r",
        "- Make changes to your theme files in Cursor\r",
        "- Sync to Local by Flywheel using `sync-all-themes.bat`\r",
        "- Test changes in your local environment\r",
        "\r",
        "### Step 2: Commit changes\r",
        "- Use Git to commit your changes:\r",
        "  ```\r",
        "  git add .\r",
        "  git commit -m \"Description of changes\"\r",
        "  ```\r",
        "\r",
        "### Step 3: Push to GitHub\r",
        "- Double-click `push-to-github.bat` from Windows Explorer\r",
        "- Follow the prompts to push your branch to GitHub\r",
        "\r",
        "### Step 4: Create Pull Request\r",
        "- Double-click `prepare-pull-request.bat` from Windows Explorer\r",
        "- Choose to open the pull request URL in your browser\r",
        "- Complete the pull request form on GitHub\r",
        "- Review and merge the pull request\r",
        "\r",
        "### Step 5: Deploy to WordPress.com\r",
        "- Double-click `wp-deploy-guide.bat` from Windows Explorer\r",
        "- Follow the step-by-step guide for deploying to WordPress.com\r",
        "\r",
        "## Alternative Manual Upload Method\r",
        "\r",
        "If GitHub Deployments isn't working as expected, you can use the manual upload method:\r",
        "\r",
        "1. Double-click `export-theme.bat` to create a .zip file of your child theme\r",
        "2. Log in to WordPress.com dashboard\r",
        "3. Go to Appearance → Themes → Add New → Upload Theme\r",
        "4. Upload the .zip file from the `exports` folder\r",
        "5. Activate the theme\r",
        "\r",
        "## Troubleshooting\r",
        "\r",
        "- If GitHub Deployments fails, check the deployment logs in WordPress.com dashboard\r",
        "- Ensure your child theme has the correct `GitHub Theme URI` in style.css\r",
        "- Verify both parent and child themes are included in your repository\r",
        "- Test with manual upload if GitHub Deployments continues to fail"
      ]
    }
  ],
